# CMS inventory sync

Live website + admin CMS read **Cloudflare D1**. `app/cms/seed-products.ts` is the repo mirror. The two are kept in step automatically while `npm run dev` runs (see "CMS sync" in the README); when it does not, the sync commands do it.

## Is the dev server running?

Check with `lsof -nP -iTCP:5173 -sTCP:LISTEN`.

- **Running:** make the change in the **local admin** (`http://localhost:5173/admin`, or log in with `POST /dashboard/session` using `DASHBOARD_USERNAME` / `DASHBOARD_PASSWORD` from `.dev.vars` and `PUT /api/admin/products/{id}`), or edit `app/cms/seed-products.ts` directly. Either way the dev server pushes it to production within seconds and leaves the seed file as the diff to commit. Do not run a sync command as well.
- **Not running:** edit `app/cms/seed-products.ts`, then `npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --products` (needs `npx wrangler login`). The local database catches up the next time the dev server starts. If the production admin may have been used since the last commit, pull first (`npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --pull --products`) so the push does not overwrite that edit.

## Adding a new product

1. Put the slab photos in `seed/media/` as `<cert>_front.jpg` and `<cert>_back.jpg`, then `npm run cms:seed-media`.
2. Add a row for each photo to `seed/cms-media.json` with `"folder": "Slabs"` — every product image belongs in the **Slabs** folder of the media library, never at the top level (`npm test` checks this).
3. Add the product to `app/cms/seed-products.ts` (`images` are `/media/<cert>_front.jpg`, `/media/<cert>_back.jpg`), then sync as described above.

## Two paths — always finish both sides of the mirror

### A. User asks in chat to change inventory (price, sold, concept, copy, Marktplaats/Vinted URL, …)

Do **all** of these before saying done:

1. Change the product as described above, and update tests that assert those fields.
2. If the card has `marktplaatsUrl` and price/listing status changed → update or delete Marktplaats per `marktplaats-listings` rules (Vraagprijs = shop − €0,01).
3. If the card has `vintedUrl` and price/listing status changed → update or delete the Vinted listing per `vinted-listings` rules (same price as the current Marktplaats Vraagprijs).

### B. User changed something in the admin CMS

Admin saves already update **live D1 / website**, and a running dev server writes them into the seed file on its own. If no dev server was running, pull (`npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --pull --products`) before touching the seed file.

1. Update tests if assertions no longer match.
2. If they changed **price** (or took a listing down) on a card with `marktplaatsUrl` or `vintedUrl` → still update Marktplaats/Vinted the same way as path A. CMS does not touch either marketplace.

## Commands

| Command | Direction |
| --- | --- |
| `npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --products` | seed → production D1 |
| `npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --pull --products` | production D1 → seed |
| `npm run cms:push` / `npm run cms:pull` | same for the local database, all parts |
| `npm run cms:push:remote` / `npm run cms:pull:remote` | production, all parts (a full push also syncs media in R2) |

## Do not

- Stop after editing `seed-products.ts` alone when no dev server is running.
- Run seed→D1 sync when seed is behind CMS without pulling first (that overwrites live CMS edits).
- Assume deploy alone refreshed product rows (only empty DB seed + one-shot `cmsSeedVersion` migrations do that).
